{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787323360046815001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"aciduric-enhanced-piranha","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6ccc49c6df89aac7f67d53394bcc37eebb81f837c0e9340b5d94102b56179f98","event_uuid":"e7505781-ff62-45bb-b168-295927214aa6","position":{"commit_sha":"11d3e8c3603768c2edb7b0cf00a03897e3f3d0b0","position":"1787320331934232001-e7505781-ff62-45bb-b168-295927214aa6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"06061c0284fea7ded29f4f54913d10b52fa1f24bd845a05355aeb3b2c1f372d1","event_uuid":"21dba019-8ec0-4ab9-bbd4-e4634c885ac7","position":{"commit_sha":"3ee1b5f6236bafb23f3753153cb8769bcd772f22","position":"1787320380469420001-21dba019-8ec0-4ab9-bbd4-e4634c885ac7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787320331934232001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"21dba019-8ec0-4ab9-bbd4-e4634c885ac7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f"}],"description":"## Observation\n`scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is wired into CI as its own step\n(`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:157`, \"comment-hygiene gate\") and is covered\nlocally only by `tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py::test_the_real_tree_is_clean`,\nwhich runs in the **full** suite. It is **not** in `make lint`.\n\nVerified: `grep -n 'comment_hygiene' Makefile` returns nothing; the only hits are in the\nworkflow.\n\n## Why it matters\nThe Makefile already states the opposite policy for a sibling gate, at `Makefile:218-220`:\n\n> Env-var registry drift (bug: fail-closed os.environ scan). CI runs this in the\n> `Env-var registry drift gate` step of .github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml and via\n> tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py; running it here makes the local\n> verdict agree with CI instead of surfacing staleness only in the full suite (~0.55s).\n\nComment-hygiene is in exactly the \"surfacing only in the full suite\" state that the drift\ngate deliberately escaped, and for the same reason it should not be: it is **fast**\n(sub-second on the full tree locally) and its findings are trivially fixable at authoring\ntime.\n\n## Measured cost\nBug 84c7 (`surprised-convincing-gopher`, change 1999) took a `Verified -1` on patchset 1\nfor 8 bare commit SHAs in comments the author added. `make lint` returned exit 0 on that\nexact tree, so the local fast gate gave a clean verdict over a tree CI rejected. It cost a\nfull review cycle: two red jobs (`lint + type-check` at 1m10s and `pytest` at 15m09s, the\nlatter's ONLY failure being the hygiene guard test out of 15169 passing).\n\n## Options (decide on evidence)\n- **Add it to `make lint`** next to `check_config_ownership.py` /\n  `gen_env_registry.py --check`, mirroring the documented drift-gate rationale. Cheapest and\n  most consistent; confirm the runtime is genuinely negligible on the full tree first.\n- **Leave as-is** and instead document in CONTRIBUTING/AGENTS that comment-hygiene is\n  CI-only, if there is a deliberate reason it was kept out of the fast gate (e.g. it was\n  intended to be a slow whole-tree scan). Check the introducing ticket for that intent before\n  assuming there is none.\n\nNote the CI step is otherwise well-behaved: unlike the `_optionality.yml` step in\n`anxious-resistant-urson`, it carries a proper if-present guard for trees that predate it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The introducing ticket for `check_comment_hygiene.py` is checked for deliberate intent\n      to keep it out of `make lint`, and the finding recorded here.\n- [ ] Either the gate runs in `make lint` (with its measured runtime recorded), or the\n      CI-only status is documented where contributors will see it.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full suite stay green.\n\n## Provenance\nFound by taking a `Verified -1` on change 1999 for a gate that `make lint` could not\nsurface. Not folded into that change: bug 84c7 is scoped to the KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS\ntable->tree invariant, and editing the lint target is a different concern.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2d9a-78c5-5f87-4a22","ticket_type":"task","title":"comment-hygiene gate is reachable locally only via the full suite, not make lint","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e7505781-ff62-45bb-b168-295927214aa6","21dba019-8ec0-4ab9-bbd4-e4634c885ac7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787323360046815001,"uuid":"67696945-0688-4c91-b347-e41b1ecacb1b"}